###Pure
// Replicates the findCommonType nested if(pair, pair, ...) pattern where
// Nil_GT inside the | Nil lambda's returnType loses its canonical UDPGT-PE
// reference. Java direct's _GenericType.reconcileInferred rebuilds the inner
// Nil_GT as a fresh inline UDGT during type reconciliation — so the printed
// classifier hierarchy shows `Class<Nil>` (no canonical anchor) instead of
// `Class<@Nil@>` (canonical anchor). This test PINS DOWN the canonical
// preservation expectation; it currently FAILS on Java direct, exposing the
// drift that the @X@ printer annotation now makes visible.
function test::nilInNestedIf(b: Boolean[1]): Type[0..1]
{
    if([pair(|$b, |Nil), pair(|true, |Nil)], | Nil);
}

